(A Digital Platform Targeting Symptom Burden in Inflammatory Bowel Disease: Study Protocol) Tj
T*
(for Evaluating Clinical Effectiveness, Cost-Effectiveness, and Implementation) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Patients with inflammatory bowel disease frequently experience persistent pain, fatigue,) Tj
T*
(and bowel dysfunction despite medical optimization. Digital self-management platforms) Tj
T*
(offer potential for symptom-focused support, yet rigorous effectiveness and economic) Tj
T*
(evaluation remains limited. This protocol describes a prospective parallel-group) Tj
T*
(randomized trial comparing digital-facilitated self-management against standard care in) Tj
T*
(approximately 780 adults with inflammatory bowel disease. The intervention comprises) Tj
T*
(interactive modules addressing pain management, energy conservation, and continence) Tj
T*
(strategies, delivered via secure platform with periodic facilitator contact. Participants) Tj
T*
(will be randomized 1:1 to intervention or care-as-usual. Primary clinical outcomes include) Tj
T*
(disease-specific quality-of-life metrics and global symptom improvement at 12 months.) Tj
T*
(Secondary outcomes include healthcare utilization, out-of-pocket costs, work productivity,) Tj
T*
(and quality-adjusted life years. Economic analysis will assess incremental cost-) Tj
T*
(effectiveness ratios from both healthcare system and societal perspectives. Baseline) Tj
T*
(characteristics, disease phenotype, and treatment intensity will be examined as potential) Tj
T*
(effect modifiers.) Tj
